 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not necessarily. Lots of people do it and enjoy it. The key things to check are a dry room, no wind, and little distance. Good idea. You can use gloves, either full gloves that stay on or armsleeves you can slip in and out of. There are winter bike trousers too. That's the smart move. The bus is really quite comfortable once you' on it. Not necessarily, but deep channelled road tyres handle well even if they' rather bald. What matters more is not over ambitiousing your ride and stopping regularly.",
